<!--
  Detection : RDP Brute Force (Windows)
  Lab       : soc-home-lab (Wazuh 4.9.2, Win10 Target + Sysmon)
  Install   : /var/ossec/etc/rules/local_rules.xml
              then: systemctl restart wazuh-manager
  Rule ID   : 100001 (custom range 100000+)

  Description:
    100001  Correlation rule. Fires when 5 or more events matching the
            built-in rule 60122 (Logon Failure - Unknown user or bad
            password) are seen within 300 seconds. Level 12.

  MITRE ATT&CK:
    T1110      Brute Force
    T1110.001  Password Guessing

  Why override the MITRE mapping:
    Wazuh's built-in rule 60122 is tagged with T1531 (Account Access
    Removal) by default, which does not describe a failed-logon event.
    This custom rule re-tags the correlated activity with the correct
    Credential Access techniques (T1110 / T1110.001) instead of
    inheriting the built-in rule's tag.

  Validated against a real run:
    - Attack: Hydra (rdp module) from Kali against Target-host over RDP.
    - Target logs showed Event ID 4625 with LogonType 3 (Network), not
      LogonType 10 (RemoteInteractive). With NLA enabled on the target,
      Windows logs the pre-authentication failure as LogonType 3 because
      a full RDP session is never established.
    - Hydra's RDP module could not complete the run against this target
      ("all children were disabled due to too many connection errors");
      no successful logon (Event 4624) was observed in this run.
    - This rule still fired correctly on the failed-logon burst, which is
      the detection goal regardless of whether the brute force succeeds.

  Investigation: ../investigations/rdp-brute-force.md

  Future work:
    - A follow-up rule for a successful logon (Event 4624, LogonType 3 or
      10) shortly after this one fires would flag a likely compromise.
      Not included here yet because it has not been validated against a
      real successful logon in this lab.
-->
<group name="windows,rdp,authentication_failures,custom,">

  <rule id="100001" level="12" frequency="5" timeframe="300">
    <if_matched_sid>60122</if_matched_sid>
    <description>Custom: RDP Brute Force Attack Detected (MITRE T1110)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1110</id>
      <id>T1110.001</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>brute_force,credential_access,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
